[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-101622"] :question/problem "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=-1,{x}_{3}=3,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $2.$ Find $P(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=-1$ and ${x}_{3}=3,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=2,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =2(x-(-1))(x-(-1))(x-3) \\\\  & =2(x+1)(x+1)(x-3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x+1)(x+1)(x-3) & =2({x}^{2}+2x+1)(x-3) \\\\  & =2({x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+2{x}^{2}-6x+x-3) \\\\  & =2({x}^{3}-{x}^{2}-5x-3) \\\\  & =2{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-10x-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=2{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-10x-6.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-104469"] :question/problem "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-5,$ ${x}_{2}=0,$ and ${x}_{3}=1,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $-2.$ Find $P(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=-5,$ ${x}_{1}=0,$ and ${x}_{3}=1,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=-2,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =-2(x-(-5))(x-0)(x-1) \\\\  & =-2x(x+5)(x-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x(x+5)(x-1) & =-2x({x}^{2}+4x-5) \\\\  & =-2({x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-5x) \\\\  & =-2{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+10x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=-2{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+10x.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-104471/selection/3de718b09ed4d37155af2fd6e2e2f84122ea7854b817020c7a804ac6c78b7341" :answer/id #uuid "0754b73c-fa0c-567e-acd4-6eaaf32f9cb6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5{x}^{3}-25{x}^{2}-15x+45" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104471/selection/fc550