orrect "q-275172/field-3/897ce4c7911f99b265ba23f864c4eaa9aec53942cbd2bbe07376f6b49ce12837" :answer-field/choices ["q-275172/field-3/897ce4c7911f99b265ba23f864c4eaa9aec53942cbd2bbe07376f6b49ce12837"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-275172/field-4/8cd557fa143c2616f01a8df1d19e854fea26be776628dc106639661d1b774491" :answer/id #uuid "df2c67de-7b80-500f-a702-aaae9e6c8136" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "65" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275172/field-4" :answer-field/id #uuid "ea785752-b49f-58e4-8622-574073534e7d" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-275172/field-4/8cd557fa143c2616f01a8df1d19e854fea26be776628dc106639661d1b774491" :answer-field/choices ["q-275172/field-4/8cd557fa143c2616f01a8df1d19e854fea26be776628dc106639661d1b774491"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-275172" :question/id #uuid "96a0a3e4-159f-50b4-bed9-d153893e944f" :question/math-academy-id "q-275172" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/assets/210d2120771bef60b0db703a04a06df395225a0c9a884faf012d55f0ed1f60d6.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of the cubic polynomial $f(x).$ Find $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $5.$\n\n$f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}${x}^{3}\\,-$\n{{field-2}}${x}^{2}\\,+$\n{{field-3}}$x\\,-$\n{{field-4}}" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=1$ and ${x}_{2,3}=3\\pm 2\\text{i}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=5.$ Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =5(x-1)(x-(3+2\\text{i}))(x-(3-2\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(x-1)(x-(3+2\\text{i}))(x-(3-2\\text{i})) & = \\\\ 5(x-1)({x}^{2}-x(3-2\\text{i})-x(3+2\\text{i})+(3+2\\text{i})(3-2\\text{i})) & = \\\\ 5(x-1)({x}^{2}-6x+13) & = \\\\ 5({x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}+13x-{x}^{2}+6x-13) & = \\\\ 5{x}^{3}-35{x}^{2}+95x-65.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=5{x}^{3}-35{x}^{2}+95x-65.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-275172/field-1" "q-275172/field-2" "q-275172/field-3" "q-275172/field-4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e4bb90c5-2794-5657-8f0b-45eb64873e03"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-275172"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-17407/selection/bc0a5c3b4213f193daf9d3c232fdb07f8d3ecd4d40108b3085c39341b89086d0" :answer/id #uuid "a4bd8db2-376d-5ea8-89f5-d2d2a68965c5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{3}-5{x}^{2}+16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-17407/selection/49129c49112e9ef12055d04e5212e0609fb12f4065ece0b1d6f9c745a6f7c4dd" :answer/id #uuid "56171563-0615-5fb3-b854-9300e0b02d03" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-17407/selection/b549629f63f589ba89b43b007cc96b1e7177004544d97a595428e2288f378e1e" :answer/id #uuid "ef6e91be-e836-5466-8026-ab7735b0b298" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+3x-18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-17407/selection/1840dcc1af09a115e8fb2f63fa4fbe365677bc8d2da32b01767eda06d538cf9b" :answer/id #uuid "27a51973-2aaf-59d1-bfad-18627b7ab64f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}+9x-36" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-17407/selection/297315a824424839c86ccc9c09f0ce1054625b3fd2527efa78fb57dce72b67bd" :answer/id #uuid "7d6e2840-e270-59a4-8d60-c00f23f258ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+10x-14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-17407/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9da7061c-555a-54eb-aa9f-d21b81deaa88" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-17407/selection/1840dcc1af09a115e8fb2f63fa4fbe365677bc8d2da32b01767eda06d538cf9b" :answer-field/choices ["q-17407/selection/bc0a5c3b4213f193daf9d3c232fdb07f8d3ecd4d40108b3085c39341b89086d0" "q-17407/selection/49129c49112e9ef12055d04e5212e0609fb12f4065ece0b1d6f9c745a6f7c4dd" "q-17407/selection/b549629f63f589ba89b43b007cc96b1e7177004544d97a595428e2288f378e1e" "q-17407/selection/1840dcc1af09a115e8fb2f63fa4fbe365677bc8d2da32b01767eda06d538cf9b" "q-17407/selection/297315a824424839c86ccc9c09f0ce1054625b3fd2527efa78fb57dce72b67bd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-17407" :question/id #uuid "54688a98-1474-5993-a7d9-b3966da03d6d" :question/math-academy-id "q-17407" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/assets/b771ac7e3d7e724b1eae9ebfc592d36a903a1fc46cc2aac5a55ea9517dc2ce12.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of a cubic polynomial $f(x).$\nFind $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $1.$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=4$ and ${x}_{2,3}=\\pm 3\\text{i}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=1.$ Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =1(x-4)(x-3\\text{i})(x-(-3\\text{i})) \\\\  & =(x-4)(x-3\\text{i})(x+3\\text{i})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-4)(x-3\\text{i})(x+3\\text{i}) & = \\\\ (x-4)({x}^{2}-x(-3\\text{i})-x(3\\text{i})+(3\\text{i})(-3\\text{i})) & = \\\\ (x-4)({x}^{2}+9) & = \\\\ {x}^{3}+9x-4{x}^{2}-36 & = \\\\ {x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}+9x-36 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)={x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}+9x-36.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-17407/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e4bb90c5-2794-5657-8f0b-45eb64873e03"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-17407"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-8799"] :question/problem "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots $x_1=x_2=2,x_3=1,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $3.$ Find $P(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${\\color{black}x_1=x_2=2}$ and ${\\color{black}x_3=1},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is ${\\color{black}a=3},$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =3(x-2)(x-2)(x-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(x-2)(x-2)(x-1) & =3({x}^{2}-4x+4)(x-1) \\\\  & =3({x}^{3}-{x}^{2}-4{x}^{2}+4x+4x-4) \\\\  & =3({x}^{3}-5{x}^{2}+8x-4) \\\\  & =3{x}^{3}-15{x}^{2}+24x-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x) = 3x^3 -15x^2+24x-12.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5792"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/assets/1c498dcdef2a71cc27117c2c0a43dd54074128ec3e5693e13a12d18b660d1cf4.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of the cubic polynomial $f(x).$ Find $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $1.$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${\\color{black}x_1= 2}$ and ${\\color{black}x_{2,3}=-2\\pm \\textrm{i}}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the cubic term is ${\\color{black}a=1}.$ \n\nTherefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =(x-2)(x-(-2+\\text{i}))(x-(-2-\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)(x-(-2+\\text{i}))(x-(-2-\\text{i})) & = \\\\ (x-2)({x}^{2}-x(-2-\\text{i})-x(-2+\\text{i})+(-2+\\text{i})(-2-\\text{i})) & = \\\\ (x-2)({x}^{2}+4x+5) & = \\\\ {x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+5x-2{x}^{2}-8x-10 & = \\\\ {x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-3x-10 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x) = x^3+2x^2-3x-10.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
